  "wikidataId": "Q130974778",
  "geometryBasis": "The mapped astronomical rotunda, adjoining fan-shaped approach and named optical telescope in the same station resolve the structure considerably north of the story pin. The owner identifies the 14-metre dome and Pentelic stone.",
  "sectionBasis": "The observatory and scholarly inventory document the 14-metre hemisphere and the 62.5 cm refractor with an 8.86 m focal length. The 1870 engraving shows the original banded optical tube, equatorial mounting and large spoked wheel.",
  "limitations": [
    "The permanent observatory footprint, crown diameter and general instrument form are grounded in primary evidence. Eave heights, exterior openings, dome shading and shutter framing are approximate.",
    "The historic refractor is posed behind an open shutter and shown as a static visual reconstruction. Fine optical mechanics, the movable floor mechanism and surrounding campus buildings are outside scope.",
    "The approach follows the mapped southern footprint, with simpler stair and pavement geometry over the original hill elevation."
